  "claims": [
    {
      "claim": "The query is N-butylscopolamine, a permanently charged quaternary ammonium tropane ester; the closest L1 structural class match, umeclidinium (also a quaternary ammonium antimuscarinic), has negligible/low oral bioavailability and ≤12% systemic availability from oral and inhaled radiolabel studies.",
      "card_ids": ["C01", "C14", "C22", "C05"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The antimuscarinic ester oxybutynin (R-enantiomer) has estimated absolute oral F ~6.7-7%, supporting low F for this ester/antimuscarinic class.",
      "card_ids": ["C08", "C34"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L3 oral exposure records for quaternary ammonium antimuscarinics show only pg/mL-level plasma concentrations after oral dosing (trospium 60 mg ER Cmax ~1.5-1.9 ng/mL and AUC24 ~23 ng·h/mL; glycopyrronium 2 mg oral Cmax 318 pg/mL; scopolamine 0.5 mg oral AUC0-24 50.77 ng·min/mL), consistent with poor oral absorption.",
      "card_ids": ["C72", "C85", "C111", "C98", "C87", "C97"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L5 provides only mechanistic gut-wall records for related quaternary ammonium antimuscarinics: OCTN2/OCT1 substrate status for ipratropium/tiotropium/trospium, ion-pair absorption for propantheline, and a trospium-ranitidine DDI showing little impact of OCT1/P-gp inhibition on oral absorption. These are not direct F measurements and do not affirmatively support F ≥20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C204", "C213", "C210", "C195", "C181", "C171"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "gut_wall_efflux_intestinal_metabolism",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C204", "C213", "C210", "C195", "C181", "C171"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No query-specific measured oral bioavailability, permeability, solubility, or intestinal metabolism data are supplied.",
    "L5 records are for other quaternary ammonium antimuscarinics, not N-butylscopolamine; no direct gut-wall efflux or intestinal metabolism measurement for the query is available.",
    "L3 exposure records lack IV comparators, so absolute F cannot be derived from them.",
    "No formulation, dose, or species match for the query is available.",
    "L5 mechanistic records (OCTN2/OCT1 substrate status, ion-pair absorption, trospium-ranitidine DDI) do not establish F ≥20%."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Prediction remains low. The query is N-butylscopolamine, a permanently charged quaternary ammonium tropane ester; transferable L1 evidence from umeclidinium (negligible/low oral F, ≤12% systemic availability) and oxybutynin (~7% absolute F) supports F <20%. L3 oral exposure records for quaternary ammonium antimuscarinics show only pg/mL-level plasma concentrations after oral dosing. L5 adds only mechanistic gut-wall records for related quaternary ammonium antimuscarinics; these are not direct F measurements and do not affirmatively support F ≥20%. Confidence remains high."
}

